+## AAL2 Step-Up
 
-### Multi-Factor Authentication and Recovery Codes
+All administrative surfaces and sensitive mutations require Authenticator Assurance Level 2 (AAL2) step-up authentication (`Depends(require_admin_aal2)`).
+
+![WebSudo Replay Active](images/slice1-websudo-replay-active.png)
+
+### WebSudo Replay Architecture
+
+When an administrator attempts a sensitive action (such as saving a newly configured LDAP card, modifying role bindings, or minting API tokens) after their session has fallen back to AAL1:
+1. The backend responds with HTTP 403 `AAL2_REQUIRED`.
+2. The frontend intercepts the response, captures the pending mutation in an in-memory queue, and opens the WebSudo elevation modal over the dirty editor drawer.
+3. The administrator enters their password, TOTP code, or touches their passkey to elevate to AAL2.
+4. Upon successful elevation, the pending mutation is automatically replayed with the newly elevated session credentials. Dirty form inputs are preserved without data loss.
+5. The elevated AAL2 session remains active for a sliding window of 900 seconds (15 minutes). Explicit step-down is available via `POST /api/v1/auth/aal2/drop`.
+
