+## Capability Bitmask and Deny Precedence
+
+To guarantee high-performance authorization evaluation without recursive database queries, 👍kanban compiles permissions into an authoritative 8-bit integer bitmask:
+
+```python
+class Capability(IntFlag):
+    NONE = 0
+    VIEW = 1 << 0        # 1
+    COMMENT = 1 << 1     # 2
+    EDIT = 1 << 2        # 4
+    TRANSITION = 1 << 3  # 8
+    LINK = 1 << 4        # 16
+    SHARE = 1 << 5       # 32
+    ADMIN = 1 << 6       # 64
+    DELETE = 1 << 7      # 128
+    ALL = 0xFF           # 255
+```
+
+### Absolute DENY Precedence Rule
+
+When computing effective access for a user or agent across inherited groups and direct ACLs:
+
+$$\text{Effective Capability} = (\text{Inherited} \cup \text{Direct Allow}) \setminus \text{Direct Deny}$$
+
+If any role, group, or explicit resource ACL specifies an explicit `DENY` mask for a capability, that capability is mathematically stripped (`allow & (~deny)`). An explicit `DENY` takes precedence over all administrative tiers below Server Administrator.
+
